  "id": "indirect-near",
  "title": "a bounded near ray observes a small emitter and its independent first-ray reference",
  "binding": "Source preparation: the authored 0.12m red metallic emitter sits 0.18m above a white receiver. Metal removes reflected feedback but leaves emission 1*red*white=red; Feedback remains enabled and requires the actual predecessor and proof. The companion changes only emissive 1 to 0 and must fail the same positive red-emission bound while holding zero. Both backends use the shared pointer and one fenced explanation. That one response must report NearHit/Resolved, its pre-material emission and the independent fixed-first-ray reference together; absent transport provenance or unsupported sources refuse rather than use the cache reference. Pointer 64,64 and first explanation admission are provisional until observed in the real World; a miss/nonadmitted phase fails and requires an authored station correction. This initial fixture does not establish the separate diffuse-bleed, finite furnace, sealed-room, gloss/fog or P15 temporal outcomes, which remain owed in their prepared scenes. The counters extraction uses the actual views/indirect-near detail row after the world node. These are newest completed submission counts, not cumulative warm-up totals; no measured ceiling is invented.",
